    <!-- Watch Out For -->
    <section class="exam-section" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #fff3cd 0%, #ffe5a0 100%); border-left-color: #ffc107;">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation section-icon" style="color: #856404;"></i> Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Memory vs Storage:</strong> Using the terms interchangeably (e.g., "I need more memory on my hard drive").</li>
            <li><strong>The "Cloud":</strong> Thinking the cloud is an abstract "space" rather than a physical server farm managed via virtualisation.</li>
            <li><strong>Multi-core performance:</strong> Assuming a 4-core processor is simply 4x faster than a single core, ignoring software-level threading limitations.</li>
            <li><strong>Register updates:</strong> Believing the PC updates at the end of the cycle rather than immediately after the fetch.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

